WEBVTT

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.360
And that about does it for
essential information-paca.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.480
Any questions-paca?

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.860
I-I think I'm okay.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.820
Thank you for shopping here-paca!

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.660
Hello, I'm Kurata Ami.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:44.950
We're on a two-day cycling trip

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.520
and have come all the way to Shimanami Kaido!

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.440
Shimanami Kaido is amazing.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:04.540
Isn't it interesting how the sea is surrounded by land?

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.640
Yeah, I've never seen scenery like this.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:10.690
Isn't it a beautiful place?

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:11.790
Yes!

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.010
If we go up this blue line,
we'll reach Imabari, right?

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.010
Yeah, but not only that.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:24.330
There are bicycle stands throughout the course

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:28.840
with rest stops and toilets at each cycling terminal

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:32.030
and various services,
including air pumps and potable water.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:38.030
Shimanami Kaido sounds like a paradise for cyclists!

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:42.540
And you'll get to find out
everything this paradise entails.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.390
Say, Ami...

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:47.410
I heard you tried to lug a ton of stuff with you on your way here.

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:49.920
Ah, well...

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.670
Hey, Ami...

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.710
What's with all that stuff?

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:58.180
Huh? Stuff?

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.490
Hinako-san, how come both of you are carrying so little?

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.810
Can you show us what you brought?

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:09.150
A change of clothes, street clothes other than your jersey, and pajamas?

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.270
Clothes are important, right?

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.990
Toiletries, towel, hair dryers, and all the attachments.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
These are must-haves for an overnight trip, right?

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.060
And a pillow and stuffed animal.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:23.950
A pillow you're used to helps you sleep comfortably.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.340
You don't need all this for a cycling trip!

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.940
Just your jersey, a change of clothes, and a towel is all you need!

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.080
Plus an extra set of underwear.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.150
Animal print, huh?

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.630
Such cute underwear!

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.820
Don't spread them out in public!

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:51.390
On a cycling trip like this,
it's standard to bring just the bare minimum.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:55.900
Ami-chan, we're almost at Innoshima Bridge.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.530
Once we cross that, we'll be in Innoshima.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.040
Innoshima Bridge!

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:15.940
Wow, they put the bridge that high?

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.400
That's pretty amazing.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:23.800
We have to climb all the way up there, right?

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:28.500
Do we have to do that each time
we cross between islands?

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.810
Well, yeah.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.680
No way...

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.920
I thought Shimanami Kaido was a cyclist's paradise...

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:41.040
No one told me it'll be full of ups and downs!

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.070
Hang in there, Ami!

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.710
Ahh! I was betrayed!

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.700
Don't worry.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:55.960
The average slope to the bridge
is only 3%, it's an easy hill.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:04:00.470
There haven't been any sharp
ups or downs so far, have there?

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.400
Y-Yes...

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.390
I'm ashamed of myself for panicking.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:07.950
But...

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.730
It really is an easy ride.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:16.510
This place really was built with cyclists in mind.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:27.490
This bridge is...

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:35.720
Wow! There's a path under the bridge road!

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.610
It really is amazing.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:41.090
It's a first for me too.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.260
Isn't it fun?

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:45.760
But...

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:48.390
But when you think about it,

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.570
we're just crossing a bridge,

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:56.700
but it's such a strange feeling to be able to cross the ocean with just bicycles!

00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:00.400
True, this is a rare experience.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:05.530
Anyway, we'll be in Innoshima soon.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:10.080
There's a place I really want to check out.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.920
A detour...?

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.170
It's delicious!

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:25.930
The sweet and sour balance of the
navy bean paste and the Hassaku citrus is perfect!

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.290
It truly is!

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.810
Yummy...

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:35.210
This Hassaku daifuku...

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:37.840
is to die for!

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.440
Take it easy, will you?

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:44.440
Do you have any other recommendations for places like this further on?

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.870
Of course!

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:50.650
There are so many great things to try.
Too many to count!

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.120
Gelato, croquettes...

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.940
soft-serve ice cream...

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.870
And it's not just food.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.870
Shio ramen...

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.130
If you want to see something unusual,
there's a bicycle shrine.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.130
A bicycle shrine?!

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.880
There's one here in Innoshima.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.300
It's a bit off the course though.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.890
But we have lots of time.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.890
You can purchase charms for your bicycle.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:19.220
We can make a stop there for good luck.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.400
Okay, shall we get going?

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.470
Yes!

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:01.290
Shimanami Kaido is the best!

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:04.290
The rides are fun,

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:09.050
the baths feel wonderful,
and the food tastes great.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.500
This is paradise!

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:18.110
Saki-san, you're amazing.

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:19.560
What do you mean?

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.560
You rode all the way here alone,
without relying on public transport.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:28.620
Well, I did it over four days,
so it was pretty leisurely.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.990
Why don't you take the train partway?

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:36.950
Well, I enjoy cycling...

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:41.950
But I guess the main reason is that I have a goal.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.580
A goal?

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.460
PBP.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:48.330
I want to ride in the Paris-Brest-Paris.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.370
Paris-Brest-Paris?

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:54.180
Isn't that a dessert?

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:58.220
No! Although there is a connection.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:02.780
Paris-Brest-Paris is the top brevet held in Paris.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:05.980
Actually, Yayoi and I have that as a goal too.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:09.050
They have brevets in France too?!

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.610
Ami, that's where they started...

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:14.810
But how will you get your bicycles over there?

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:18.120
You just pack it on a plane.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:21.120
Pack it on... a plane?!

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:29.560
Isn't that amazing, Aoi-chan!
This thing is worldwide!

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:30.630
Yeah.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:38.640
Here I thought my world had expanded so much, but...

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:42.890
Is this Paris-Brest-Paris that big of a deal?

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.640
Well, it is the home of the brevet.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.110
The Paris-Brest-Paris...

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:52.640
is only held once every four years,
it's like the Olympics of brevets.

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:55.650
It's like a festival there.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:57.910
The Olympics of brevets?

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:03.290
It's from Paris to Brest and back,
1200 kilos in 90 hours.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:04.570
A thousand...?

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:09.290
I doubt I'll ever make that in my lifetime.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:13.800
Knowing you, Ami, you'll want to try it one day.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:18.300
All the locals come out to
cheer you on as a whole country.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:22.800
Along the course, perfect strangers hand out refreshments to riders.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:28.560
And you get to see beautiful scenery in a foreign land.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:32.030
Just once, I'd like to participate in it.

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:39.210
Well, there are a lot of hurdles though.

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:40.610
That's for sure.

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:42.870
But you want to go, right?

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:44.260
Well, sure.

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:45.870
Of course!

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:50.350
Yayoi-san, Hinako-san, and Saki-san...

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:52.620
Their eyes are sparkling.

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:57.490
It must be a wonderful brevet.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.660
Huh?

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.250
What should we do?

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:43.400
Further up, there's a place to board the ferry.

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.340
But that goes towards Onomichi.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.050
We're turning back?

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:54.770
We can't even ride,
let alone reach our destination.

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:01.050
Aoi-chan...

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:03.530
It's raining hard, but...

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:07.770
isn't there a way we can keep going in the rain?

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:11.540
Well, there are ways, but...

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.990
What do you think?

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.380
Can we?

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:20.880
Why're you looking at me like that?

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:24.640
Ahh, you two have promise.

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:31.330
In fact, there are times we ride through rain like today's in a fléche or brevet.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:32.890
Really?

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:40.400
That's why I think getting accustomed to cycling in the rain would be a great idea.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.900
I think so too!

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.540
Aoi-chan, what do you think?

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:47.560
I'm fine with doing whatever you want, Ami.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.160
Just...

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:52.520
don't catch a cold from the rain.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:58.040
So we'll just ride with raincoats.
They sell them at convenience stores.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:03.670
The roads will be slippery from the rain,
so it'll be hard to brake. Please be careful.

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.930
I understand.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.280
Oh, I see!

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:15.300
The rain won't bother us with these.

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:16.380
See?

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:17.710
Okay!

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.460
My first ride in the rain!

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:23.050
Let's go!

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:27.570
Ami, watch out for the grating!

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:28.950
Huh, gra...?

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:36.050
This is nothi-...!

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:41.850
Ami!

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.940
I thought I was going to split!

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.110
Are you okay?

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:49.090
My road bike!

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:53.120
It looks okay at a glance.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.820
Aww, the bracket is bent.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:08.360
Oh, my.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:11.140
Wh-Wh-Wh-What should I do?

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.280
Let me see.

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:21.560
There, all fixed.

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:24.130
Just like that?

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:26.440
Thank goodness!

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:29.210
I totally thought I'd broken it.

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:31.390
Thank you so much!

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:34.460
No need for that. It was a simple fix.

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:38.140
It happens quite often.
We'll show you how to fix it later.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.910
Thank you. I'd like that.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:41.660
Still...

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:44.650
It's so easy to slip...

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:48.480
It's quite scary, riding in the rain.

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:49.400
Oh no,

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:54.810
mainly, you just have to watch for metallic lids, like manhole covers, and the white lines.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:57.490
If your weight shifts to the side, you'll slip.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:15:00.920
If you can't avoid it, ride straight through it.

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:03.920
Once you've tried it, you'll know.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:04.940
Okay.

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:23.050
Is that...?

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:29.970
I can do it.

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:31.720
Do just as she said.

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:33.530
Straight ahead.

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:41.130
Okay!

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:46.090
Now that I know what to watch for,

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.630
I think I can ride as usual.

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:55.860
In the rain, I can really smell the earth.

00:15:56.650 --> 00:16:00.410
It's like being enveloped in nature!

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.880
Wow...

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:29.800
It's amazing!

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:31.380
It really is!

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:34.600
Aren't you glad you rode through the rain?

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:35.390
Yes!

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.640
If it's as wonderful as this...

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:42.320
riding in the rain is fun!

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:50.860
I'm covered in sweat.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.630
I'm completely drenched under the raincoat.

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:58.240
Your backpack probably made you especially steamy.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:02.630
Yes, my back's all wet.

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:06.270
That's why it's easier to pack light.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:08.750
What's wrong?

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:13.760
My leg... feels a little sore and itchy...

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:17.160
Ami, you're wearing leg warmers the usual way?

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:18.640
Uh, yes...

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:21.200
That can irritate the skin.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:27.400
You know how leg warmers have an
elastic band so they don't slide down?

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.630
That scrapes the skin raw.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:32.960
Especially when the skin gets soft from the rain.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:35.070
Worst case, it can start bleeding.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:40.810
Once, the elastic band stuck to my skin
and peeled the skin off where it was.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:44.040
Wh-What should I do then?!

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:48.290
Fold the elastic part so that it's not directly on your skin.

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:50.540
Like this. See?

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:54.920
Saki-san, not here!

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:57.200
It's fine, I don't mind it!

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:00.050
But you're making <i>me</i> embarrassed!

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:03.190
Okay then, let's get back to it.
Just one last push to our goal.

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:04.180
Yes.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.110
That's right...

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:11.060
I was so worried when you
made me lighten my pack, but...

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.810
There weren't any problems, were there?

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:13.440
None at all.

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:18.950
I learned that you can travel really far
without much stuff when you ride a bike.

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:23.150
But that's not all you learned.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:28.480
Overnight cycling plans can be applied to long-distance rides too.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:33.870
Stay at an inn, then set out in the morning.

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:36.590
If you keep repeating that, you can go a long way.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:40.970
Ahh, you're right.
If I take my time, I think I can make it.

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:44.970
If you think that way,
your world suddenly expands, right?

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.190
Yes!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.660
I see!

00:18:56.660 --> 00:19:01.490
Traveling a great distance
wasn't that outlandish...

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:05.240
If I embrace this experience...

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.250
maybe even I can...

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:10.000
go much, much farther.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:15.000
And one day...

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.490
we can all...

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:36.040
Wow!

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:38.190
It's so pretty!

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:43.060
I never get tired of Shimanami Kaido!

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:45.800
Ami, you were able to keep up!

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:47.770
Yes.

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:50.680
Actually,

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:52.920
even before college,

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:55.470
I was interested in cycling.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:59.800
Whenever I saw you riding your bicycle...

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:04.720
I always thought it looked like fun
or that it must feel good.

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:07.590
But I'm such a klutz

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:09.810
and I was terrible at physical exercise...

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:11.530
But...

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:15.630
maybe I could manage that folding bike we just saw...

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:20.840
I was never good at anything I did.

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:26.280
But now... I've grown enough that I'm able to come all the way here with all of you.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:30.830
Saki-san!

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.350
Yayoi-san!

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:33.830
Hinako-san!

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.580
Aoi-chan!

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:38.920
I'm so glad that I discovered cycling...

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:40.560
and met all of you...

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:43.090
I'm really glad.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:46.600
I want to keep on cycling.

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:50.350
I want to keep on going with all of you.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:52.620
So...

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:55.600
Please continue to take care of me!

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:08.070
What's so funny?

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:11.830
We're on the same team.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:15.080
Let's go to many places together.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:17.830
And let's eat lots of delicious good.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:21.340
Let's have fun together, Ami.

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:45.880
Who knew there was a place like this so close!

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:52.480
Wh-What was that sound?

00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:00.270
Um, are you all right?

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:04.090
Kurata-san?

00:22:08.530 --> 00:22:10.590
Amazing, Kurata-san!

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:14.830
But what a surprise.

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:17.290
Saeki-san, you ride a road bike too?

00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:21.020
Though I just started.

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:24.860
But speaking with you
back at school,

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:29.630
you always talk about
cycling with such joy.

00:22:29.630 --> 00:22:32.810
And so... I tried it too...

00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:34.870
And it was really is fun.

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:37.400
The first time I tried out my road bike,

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:40.810
it was so light, it felt like I was flying.

00:22:40.810 --> 00:22:43.300
I might be exaggerating, but...

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:43.310
I know just how she feels.

00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:46.420
Ever since I started cycling,

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:50.440
seeing my world expand has been so much fun.

00:22:50.440 --> 00:22:53.180
And before I realized it, I was hooked.

00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:55.450
Say, Saeki-san...

00:22:55.880 --> 00:22:57.950
It's totally up to you, but...

00:23:01.140 --> 00:23:03.940
would you like to join us next time?

00:23:04.890 --> 00:23:05.950
With all of you?

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:10.740
But I'm just a beginner.

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:14.700
Don't worry! I've only been cycling for a year.

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:16.370
Besides...

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:17.980
I guarantee you,

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:22.960
it's way more fun
when you ride with others.

00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:25.980
W-Well then...

00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:28.680
I think I'd like to try...

00:23:33.610 --> 00:23:34.870
And so...

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:39.990
My cycling life, which began with a little miracle,

00:23:41.340 --> 00:23:43.830
looks like it's going to continue!
